  "data": {
    "ruleType": "army-rule",
    "summary": "With **LEAGUES OF VOTANN** as your Army Faction, your **LEAGUES OF VOTANN** units use either Hostile Acquisition or Fortify Takeover, never both, depending on your Yield points (YP):\n\n- When the battle begins, they have Hostile Acquisition until your first Command phase starts.\n- As each of your Command phases ends, they get Hostile Acquisition with under 7YP, or Fortify Takeover with 7YP or more, until your next Command phase starts.\n\nThe ability changes only then; gaining or spending YP at other times does not switch it.\n\n**Hostile Acquisition**:\n\n- The unit's models get +1 to hit when attacking an enemy unit that is in range of at least 1 objective marker.\n- The unit's Advance and **Charge rolls** can be re-rolled.\n\n**Fortify Takeover**:\n\n- While the unit is in range of at least 1 objective marker you control, its models get +1 to hit when attacking enemy units.\n- Unless the unit is a **VEHICLE**, attacks against it whose Strength exceeds its Toughness get -1 to the **Wound roll**.\n\nAs every Command phase ends, yours or your opponent's, controlling at least 1 objective marker in your deployment zone earns you 1YP. From battle round 2, you also gain 1YP for each of these that is true:\n\n- At least 1 objective marker you control is outside your deployment zone.\n- At least 2 objective markers you control are outside your deployment zone.\n- Your controlled objective markers outnumber your opponent's.\n\nIn your turn, gain these YP before checking which ability applies. A rule that costs YP can be used only if you can pay all of it; paying lowers your YP, which never goes below 0.",
